From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:30:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kk: MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=gpl, a sample mask with every sample
 links apart

With MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=gpl, a link of pipeline libraries whose
static sample mask has the bit of every rasterization sample now links
the shaders compiled on their own, as with a mask of all ones; only a
mask without one of them still compiles the whole pipeline
(fallback=sample-mask). Vulkan ignores the bits above the sample count,
and DXVK gives the mask cut to it: 0x1 at one sample, which made every
link of Hollow Knight's a whole-pipeline fallback.

The whole-pipeline path is left as it was: it still lowers a mask that
is not 0xffff into the fragment shader.

Linear: PLA-424
Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-22-kk-gpl-phone.md
Offered-upstream: not yet
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
index e9811f9..f0d9f11 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
@@ -4742,9 +4742,13 @@ kk_gpl_fragment_blocker(struct kk_device *dev,
        rp->depth_attachment_format == VK_FORMAT_UNDEFINED)
       return "depth-write";
 
-   if (state->ms && state->ms->rasterization_samples &&
-       state->ms->sample_mask != UINT16_MAX)
-      return "sample-mask";
+   /* Only the rasterization samples' bits of the mask count: DXVK gives it
+    * cut to the sample count, 0x1 at one sample */
+   if (state->ms && state->ms->rasterization_samples) {
+      const uint16_t samples = BITFIELD_MASK(state->ms->rasterization_samples);
+      if ((state->ms->sample_mask & samples) != samples)
+         return "sample-mask";
+   }
    /* Metal's alpha to coverage reads colour output 0 */
    if (state->ms && state->ms->alpha_to_coverage_enable &&
        fs->gpl_output_types[0] == 0)
